--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
dropped the body of function
--
N5008 [expr.const]/22, [temp.inst]/8: the requirement `a - b' of
subtractable<wrapper<incomplete>> names operator-<incomplete>, a constexpr
function template specialization, in an unevaluated operand: it is not
needed for constant evaluation and its definition is not instantiated.
The front end converted constexpr specializations eagerly in a constant
expression, so `w.value' of wrapper<incomplete> was an error and the body
was dropped (bin53).  This is the shape of libstdc++'s sized_sentinel_for
check of __normal_iterator<_BigBlock *, ...> in <memory_resource>.  g++ 13
and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
